# The image is built from one file, and the build is sent one file.
#
# Without this, "docker compose up --build" in a checkout sends the whole
# directory to the builder — the source, .git, anything left lying in it — and
# the Dockerfile's single COPY is then the only thing keeping it out of the
# image. One line added to that Dockerfile later would be enough to undo it.
*
!porchd
